    "title": "Fatal solo vehicle crash kills man in Stockton - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adoreil Ayoubgoulan ,\n5 hours ago\n(FOX40.COM) — A 64-year-old man is dead after a solo vehicle accident on early Wednesday morning in Stockton, according to the Stockton Police Department.\nStockton police said a man was a passenger in a car on the 2900 block of North Pershing Avenue.\nThe victim was transported to a local hospital, where he died from his injuries, officials said.\nMan wounded in a shooting incident in a business area SPD reported that traffic officers responded to the scene and took over the investigation.\nAt this time, police have not released any information regarding what caused the crash to occur.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX40 News.\n4",
    "summary": "Stockton police said a man was a passenger in a car on the 2900 block of North Pershing Avenue. The victim was transported to a local hospital, where he died from his injuries, officials said. Man wounded in a shooting incident in a business area SPD reported that traffic officers responded to the scene and took over the investigation. At this time, police have not released any information regarding what caused the crash to occur. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
